--
symbol 'read' is unknown
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/1, [temp.point]: a class template specialization is completed
only from a *definition* of the template.  CBMC used to eagerly elaborate a
specialization referenced while the template was only forward-declared (as a
by-value function parameter in a declaration, which does not require a complete
type), fabricating an empty-but-complete class that masked the members added by
the later definition ("symbol 'read' is unknown").  This is the reduced (cvise,
from preprocessed <istream>) form of the lispexpr.cpp / parser.cpp dog-food
failures (<iosfwd> forward-declares std::basic_istream before <istream> defines
it).  Fixed by definition-seen tracking (ID_C_template_defined): elaboration is
deferred until the selected template has been defined.
